      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-11-14_WidnesExaminer_art0014" n="art0014">
        <head>GREAT INDIAN</head>
        <p>THE GREAT INDIAN</p>
        <p>2s. 9D. FEMALE MEDICINE. 2. 9. Wonderful Remedy discovered by a Married Lady while- travelling in the Far Nast. Never fails to remove all irregu iarities and obstructions in two hours after all else have failed.</p>
        <p>Mrs. ll writes :—" Your Medicine acttd like a charm after two doses, although I had tried in vain other more expensive remedies for over three months." Sufferers will avoid much expense by sending at meets. 9d. for a ltttle of this extraorainary remedy. MRS. R. A. BARRINGTON. 4, Featherstone Buildings. London, W.C.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-11-14_WidnesExaminer_art0015" n="art0015">
        <head>TO LADIES.</head>
        <p>TO LADIES.</p>
        <p>MACKENZIE'S FEMAL-E--- MEDICINE Will positively remove the most obstinate Obstructions. Irregularities, ac., from any cause in twelve hours.. Guaran- tees' the most powerful and strongest upon eirth. Failure is impo--tble. It acts like magic in the most long-standing and intricate obstructions. Ladies will save time, trouble and expense by coming to an experienced Spe:uslist at first. Post tree, snider cover, securely packed, with full directions and advice (4s. 61.) FOUR SHILLINGS AND SIXPENCE, WITH WRITIEN GUARANTEE OF CURB.</p>
        <p>Mrs. L., of High-st., Morley, near Ldseds, writes :—" One 45. 6d. packet clued me alter FOUR MONTIIV anxiety of mind, and after I had tried no less than fire different so- called remedies My sister recommended me to you, and she is equally enthusiastic. Several ladies have told me they have always been cured by you when other firms failed." Send at once or 100 paged Book of Particulars and Testi- monials, which are sworn on oath before Her Majesty's Com- missioner tor oaths to be true and genuine. All open to in- spection and £l,OOO given to any charity if one is proved not genuine. Advice willingly free. Mrs. B. MACKICNZIE, Trafford House, 83, Dawes-road,</p>
