      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-11-14_WidnesExaminer_art0019" n="art0019">
        <head>PLEASANT PARAGRAPHS.</head>
        <p>PLEASANT PARAGRAPHS.</p>
        <p>PROSPECTIVE JOY.—" Say, Chimmie, COMC down —goin' to have a bully lot o' fun." " "We've fed de goat six setlitz powders, and now we're goin' to let drink." REASONED OUT.—Co'antryman (regarding ship heavily laden aud settled low in the water) : "By jock ! If that there sea was a little higher that ship would go to the bottom."</p>
        <p>BIMETALLISM IN FicrioN.—An extract from the latest Society novel reads. "And the beautiful heiress shook her golden curls in the silver moon- light, and petulantly pursed her lips." REFLECTED GLORY.—Chiinnly " Wot's der matter wid Reddy Smith? He's so stuck up he hardly speaks to anybody." Tommy: "Why, didn't you hear ? His Uncle Bill broke out of the, penitentiary last night I " A SCEPTIC.—James (on a chilly morning) : "Hello, John !do you believe in signs?" John : " I haven't much faith in them ; for while there are two signs saying Please Close the Door,' you have left it opcn."</p>
        <p>Wir2: " If 1 had hnown you swore so before we were married, I would never have married you." The Husband. (sadly) "That's what comes of being a hypocrite. Os A COUNTRY ROAD. - First City Boy: "What's that cow got a bell on for, I wonder?" Second Ditto: "I suppose it's to tell the bicycler to look out."</p>
        <p>AS USUAL.—WiniS : "Was Jones an exhibitor at the horse show !" Wallace: " Yes—in a measure. He has made an ass of himself." Do you hear the ocean moaning, Ever moaning sad and low? 'Tis because that fat old bather Stepped upon its undertow.</p>
        <p>Gomzz : "I say, was it you who recommended that cook to my wife ? " Perez: "I believe so." Gomez: "Then I should like you to come and have dinner with us to-night." AGREEABLE,—" Let us take something," said a red-nosed man at the beach to a chance acquain- tance. " All right," was the latter's reply. " Wait until I go to the hotel and get my camera, and we'll take a picture." GETTING NEAR IT.—" Well, what do you want, sonny?" asked the grocer. "I 'most forget what mamma sent me for," replibd the perplexed little boy on the outside of the counter, "but I think it's a can of condemned milk."</p>
        <p>USEFUL HAPPINESS.—Neighbour: "I don't see what pleasure you can have in shooting at birds you never hit.' Humane Sportsman: "My plea- sure consists in thinking how happy the birds must be to be able to escape." SUICIDAL.—Miss Prion (quoting) : "'Wise men make proverbs, and fools repeat them.'" Miss Smart (musingly): "Yes. I wonder what wise man made the one you just repeated." Two WAys.—Magistrate : "You are charged, sir, with trying to commit suicide." Prisoner: "I was driven to it, your honour—driven to it by a woman." Magistrate: " Hum ! Did she refuse you or marry you?" MRS. PHILANTHRO : Tell me, my poor man, is your blindness permanent?" Mendicant (despair- ingly) : "It looks like it, lady. Times is dat bad, I don't see no chance of retiring." AN EXPLANATION. Green "By the way, Lamb, what is an option, anyhow?" Lamb: "In my experience, an option is a privilege of buying stock which is sure to go down, or of selling stock Which is sure to go</p>
        <p>WHEN ONE'S WIFE IS AWAY.—Mrs. Dorcas: "When you returned from the country, I suppose you found the place all upset? It's always that way when a man is left to keep house.' Mrs. Col,wigger : "Yes, my dear; the litter was terrible. The only place that was cleared up was the wine- cellar."</p>
        <p>A SLum.—Quester : "There goes Miner, the coal merchant. He is a man of greu.t, influence, and his words carry great weight in the community," Jesters "That's more than can be said of his</p>
        <p>waggons." A UNIVERSAL FAILING. —Friend : "Your son, I understand, has literary aspirations. Doos he write for money?" Father (feelingly); ." Unceas- ingly." LoYAL SusJscr.—Dix : " How long has your cook been with you?" Hicks: "This is the second year of her reign." CONSOLING.—An Irislainewspaper once said, in announcing an accident: "Our fellow-townsman, Mr. Hooligan, fell out of the second-storey window yesterday and broke his neck and suffered internal injuries. His friends will be glad to know that the latter are not serious."</p>
        <p>THE S URVIVO RS STAYED AWAY. —g g Are you bothered with tramps at your country place ? " "No. You see, my daughter goes to a cooking. school, and we give all that she makes to the wandering. They come once, and never come back; and of late they have been avoiding us altogether." GOOD ADVICE. —Little Grace had very curly hair, and it was a great trial to her to get it combed. One day during this process she was crying and making a greater disturbance than usual, when her mother said: "What wi 1 the neighbours say when they hear you making such a noise?" Pausing in her weeping, she replied, in broken accents "They will say, 'Why doesn't that woman spank that child ! " No TROUBLE TO SHOW GOODS. —The young man had gone into a department store to buy a fountain pen. The girl in charge of the fountain pen show- case had supplied him with a sheet of paper, a 'bottle of ink, and several of the pens, and in trying them, one after another, he covered the sheet with the words " Tempus fugit," the girl looking on with a kindly interest. 'lf you buy one and it doesn't suit you, Mr. Fugit," she remarked, "you can bring it back and change it." "There, darling, the last one," said he, as he started down the steps. He had nearly reached the gate when she called him back. "I've just been counting up," she said, "and that is an awfully unlucky number, you know." When we left an how- after he was still there. " Jonic," said the wife, looking up from the paper, "here is a writer who says wives ought to do all in their power to render themselves attrac- tive in the eyes of their husbands. What do you think of it?" "What do I think of it? I think it is sound, common sense. That's the kind of thing to print for women's reading. Women should be taught their duty if they do not know it. [heartily agree with the sentiment." "So do I. And I may add that a new bonnet and gown would render me twice as attractive in your eyes as I am now." "Mary," said the husband, "you ithould have charge of the Alaska seal business and the fisheries Question."</p>
