      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-11-14_WidnesExaminer_art0067" n="art0067">
        <head>NATIONS HEALTH.</head>
        <p>THE NATIONS HEALTH.</p>
        <p>It is becoming more and more evident year by year to those who minutely observe the current of internal events and especially the health of the British nation that we are fast becoming a nation of Dyspeptics. The malady of dyspepsia has spread its effects not only over our own nation, but it is the prevailing malady of civi- lised life. There is no disease more prevalent or more difficult to cure. It is a disease of the stomach and as- sumes a variety of different forms in parts of the body far removed from the seat of the disease. Dyspepsia is only another name for the effects of indigestion and the different forms it assumes as its effects are kdown by various names, according to the different symptens it presents, as dyspepsia flatulence, heattburn, sick head- ache, pains in the stomach, palpitation of the heart, heart diseases,colic, dysentery, diarrhcea, &amp;c. All these id even apoplexy aud paralysis and nins tenths of the .es of convulsions in children have their source in that di -'v nutrition to which the term indigestion has beet, ',plied.</p>
        <p>Ott,er .;auses are worry, anxiety,over work, emotion, stimulants, narcotics. Many persons overload and over- tax the digestive organs which impairs their powers and renders them incapable of performing their proper func- tions. Constant overworking of the stomach must pro- duce disease of that organ. More nutriment is furnished to the tissues of the body by a small quantity of food well digested, than by a large quantity half digested. The only trust worthy and permanent remedy is Gwilym Evans's Quinine Bitters. rho Vegetable Tonic, which, acting upon the digestive organs, strengthens them and stimulates them to healthy action, and gives tone to the whole stomach imparting new life, hope, strength and happiness. It is the most successful remedy ever dis- covered, and has never failed to gain high approval and praise whenever it has been properly and fairly tried. It contains a suitable quantity of Quinine in each dose together with the Medicural Virtues of the following well-known herbs :---Sarsaparilia, Gentain. Burdock, Saffron, Lavender, and Dandelion, combined in most happy proportions, and concentrated in a pure state, as well as being scientifically prepared to be suitable to all ages, at all seasons of the year. It is Sold in Bottles, at 23. 9i. and 4s. 6d. each, by all Chemists and Patent Medicine Vendors, or Carriage Free by Parcels Post, direct from the Proprietors. Beware of imitations, see the name GWILYM EVANS, on Label, Stamp, and Bottle.</p>
        <p>QUININE BITTERS MANUFACTURING</p>
        <p>Co., LTD., LLANELLY, SOUTH WALES.</p>
